{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact 6d0ce3c72eb8ac90e226eed4bbe231f2b8d69b62, tree 71502037bbc898b83393cf60e63c8b57d77006c7. This is a design-only review of primary a7906ea9; it grants no runtime or deployment adoption.\n\nP2 — Make the frozen Mark sufficient for exact recovery (§15.4–15.5, lines 1526 and 1582–1590). The manifest stores entry ranges and retained-input digests. Mark adds parent, cutoff, manifest bytes, commit ID and time, then promises a rebuild without reading the scope's storage. None of these supplies new entry/input bytes or a durable Git object closure. Reset after Mark but before those objects reach the remote leaves the parent unable to reconstruct them. A digest or rebuild-mismatch check detects missing/different bytes but cannot recover them. Persist an explicitly bounded canonical byte/object closure atomically with Mark, or specify immutable recoverable dependencies and the exact bounded reads/missing-data contract. Keep the one-pending-commit, same-cutoff and exact-object guarantees. A3 must reset before remote object availability, add later live input, and reconstruct the original commit using only the named retained dependencies; fresh enumeration must not silently substitute new state.\n\nP2 — Include the full Replay dependency closure in cutoff selection (§15.3, lines 1485–1497). The inventory names uses, rules/snapshots, and definition/value digests in act fields. It misses the genesis declaration named by input.seed.definition and values referenced through outcome evidence. In this exact tree, verify.ts assigns the genesis declaration at line 690, #replay calls #pin before handling genesis at 1167, and the outcome path reads evidenceValues(..., input.evidence) as retained values at 1380–1405. Thus an otherwise ordinary declared genesis-only scope, or a pass first introducing an outcome-evidence value, can produce an archive without inputs its advertised clone replay requires. Define an exhaustive shared dependency inventory across input variants, including root/transitive declarations and outcome values. Explicit J2 omissions must remain separately reported. A2 should exercise those two cases using the clone alone, without service reads or implicit anchors.\n\nThe previous identity cycle is repaired: intentDigest excludes the signature, so deriving the seed before sealing is feasible. The receipt now requires its own position within the cutoff and full scope/incarnation matching; stopped/conflict and service-cutoff trust are explicit. Ref encoding, safe object-store paths, pinned archive levels, and the removal of the no-delay claim also address prior concerns.\n\nImplementation criteria remain: only an authorized establishment can validate a locator; aggregate host admission must include pre-G bootstrap and membership/watch reads; overlong legal domains need explicit stopped/refusal behavior without truncation or silent omission; receipt checking needs clone integrity and continuity before stronger prefix membership; J2 disclosures precede export. These are prospective builder/security witnesses, not additional demonstrated P2s. Preserve complete functionality; schedule estimates sequence work.\n\nCoverage: Root read the primary FIRST, directly through EOF in 29 contiguous bounded spans: 123741 bytes, SHA256 5fa349012bec93bdecc3e57a9dec7e6710146c84f1dd10722bb2da138d55c105. Root read five sealed specialist reports fully after checking their pins, and the prior negative review fully. Root's selected Replay units are fully read; verify.ts as a whole is PARTIAL. Peer coverage does not replace Root coverage. Native census against current main 70729eac shows only this note changed, with all 1572 other entries identical. No tests, builds, gate, provider or runtime probes were executed by checker. This verdict establishes Source/design conclusions only.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a7906ea9a64d92c1194786dca615ddccd1bee20e","binding":"assigned","head":"6d0ce3c72eb8ac90e226eed4bbe231f2b8d69b62","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b912025779d562d68d9d693965fb56ae8fc5e0fc\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fae322e0901ae73e961b1434c6fe55ec6d842b73\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:61414e06103cc9b8b51dab13da421eaf34e22bc7","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}